Comprehensive Revision Notes: Financial Markets and Instruments
Overview
In this session, the focus was on understanding practical applications in financial markets with a particular emphasis on company valuations using financial ratios and the dividend discount model. The instructor discussed the requirements for a financial ratio analysis assignment and walked through the valuation of listed companies using practical models and financial data. Key models covered include the Gordon Growth Model and techniques for evaluating share prices through present value calculations.

Financial Ratio Analysis Assignment
Objective: Conduct a financial ratio analysis of a listed company.
Requirements:
Choose any listed company (Indian or international, excluding banks and service-startups).
Perform analyses on two financial years using company's balance sheet, income statement, and cash flow statement.
Ratios to compute: Liquidity, Solvency, Working Capital Efficiency, and Profitability.
Interpret results and provide investment recommendations.
Submission: Detailed report (3 pages maximum) by October 2nd, 11:50 PM in PDF format following specified naming conventions.
